# == Projects
#
# - *Five-Stage Pipelined RISC-V CPU & xv6-Inspired OS* (Mar 2024 -- May 2025). Designed a five-stage pipelined RISC-V CPU in SystemVerilog with BTB\/BHT branch prediction, a 2 KiB cache, and an Sv39 MMU; brought up a minimalist xv6-inspired OS with page-table virtual memory, trap\/interrupt handling, mode transitions, and a FAT32-style file system.
# - *Needle: A Compiler from C to RISC-V* (Mar 2025 -- Jun 2025). Built an end-to-end compiler for a C subset using Flex and Bison (AST, semantic analysis, IR generation) and a RISC-V code generator handling calling conventions and control flow.

== Skills

- *Programming Languages:* Python, C\/C\+\+, SystemVerilog.
- *Machine Learning Tools:* PyTorch, einx\/einops, Gymnasium, Stable-Baselines3.
- *Systems & Infra:* Linux, Git, Shell Scripting, Docker, Slurm.
- *Writing & Typesetting:* LaTeX, Typst, TikZ.

I maintain an [https://note.v1ceversaa.cc/ open technical notebook] (400,000+ words) on computer science, mathematics, and AI as a long-term knowledge-building practice.

